{"kind":"request","text":"OAuth slice O1: make /mcp an OAuth resource server\n\nScope: slice O1 of notes/2026-11-02-hosted-mcp-oauth.md, landed at\nafdd8ee5 under checker approval e2123e2b. Hugh's order 58c6cb8e puts\nOAuth first, ahead of the next cohort.\n\nBuild what the note's part two names under Resource server, Connector\nURLs and Access tokens:\n\n- MCP_RESOURCE_URLS, validated as the note says. Every\n  MCP_CARD_ORIGINS URL must appear in it.\n- GET /.well-known/oauth-protected-resource/mcp for each connector\n  URL, with its query kept.\n- The 401 challenge with resource_metadata and scope on /mcp.\n- Access tokens \u003cagent\u003e.\u003cgrant\u003e.\u003csecret\u003e beside the static bearer,\n  checked by digest, expiry, failure window, audience equal to the\n  exact request URL, live grant, and current standing of agent, key\n  and controller, cached at most 60 seconds.\n\nO1 needs a way to issue a token for its tests before O3 exists. Use a\ntest-only issuer that writes a grant row directly. No route issues\ntokens in O1.\n\nDone when a scripted client gets 401 with the header, reads the\nmetadata for each connector URL, and calls /mcp with a test-issued\ntoken, with every O1 control in the note's part three table, a frozen\ngate and the checker's review. The static bearer and its tests keep\nworking. Hosted MCP stays closed on the deployed Workers.\n\nOrder: after the G3 configuration head, ahead of next cohort source\nchild 39487984. O1 and O2 do not depend on each other.","body":{"conditions":"The slice of notes/2026-11-02-hosted-mcp-oauth.md named in the text is built with every control the note's part three table names for it, a frozen gate passes, the checker reviews, and the head lands on main.","target_head":"afdd8ee5288a7b33c90536c9489bcfc06eafc7d9","target_ref":"refs/heads/main","target_repo":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3","to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}